elandic designers have moved  in and set up studios with shops  such as fashion label stanun  next door ziges is hard at work she's  one of the country's most successful  designers  the swedish furniture chain ikea is  among her clients  like many of their fellow icelandic  designers she studied and worked abroad  she only came back three years ago  people are very open-minded and there's  very short distance to everyone  if you want to make a prototype or if  you want to do something or collaborate  you only with one phone call you have it  done  that's not how it works in sweden to  further local design  the iceland academy of arts is offering  a course in product and textile design  previously young icelanders had to go  abroad to study design  and many stayed away after graduating  hatha helger wants to see an increase in  the number of  home-grown designers  icelandic music scene has emerged very  much during the last  20 to 30 years and it's a reality we  have  we have internationally acknowledged  music  musicians so why not designers  and who knows iceland's star designers  of tomorrow  might be sitting right here  well ever since she was a kid she's been  surrounded by vineyards and steeped  in family tradition regina menger krug  comes from the german state of heinlein  falls where her family is known  for producing some of this country's  best sparkling wine  now it's known as zecht in german and  it's made much the same way that  champagne is in france which makes it  just  as much of a party staple  germans love their sparkling wine it's  especially popular on birthdays and  other special occasions  regina mega cook's family has been  making sparkling wine for eight  generations  in dynasine in southwestern germany  her tip to becoming a successful vintner  victory you have to give into nature to  a certain extent  always go out no matter what the weather  is  puts her trust in mother nature roses  and more than 100 different herbs help  fertilize the soil  pesticides are strictly taboo the  vintner believes that if the grapes  don't succeed in the vineyard then  modern technology can't put them right  either  good wine growing sites are always a bit  finicky  they're like divas you have to take the  wines as they come  and you have to realize that at the  beginning they can still be a little  restless  maybe from fermentation but that  eventually calms down  they just need a little more time they  need tender loving care  the way we women like it right  the fine wine maturing in these barrels  riesling  chardonnay pinot blanc and pinot noir  will later become sparkling wine  begina menger krug's secret is her  moonwood barrels made from  trees felled as the moon was waning  the famous violin maker stradivari swore  by moonwood too  the wood is fine these barrels are like  a cradle for the wine  it's astonishing everyone is amazed by  how it works  a great deal of love and patience goes  into each bottle  the mega kook vineyard makes sparkling  wine the classic french way like  champagne  the wine ferments with yeast in the  bottle for nine months to  two years then the yeast is removed  this wine has been fermenting for more  than 30 years and it's still drinkable  it's also fascinating that as long as  the yeast remains in the wine  the sparkling wine doesn't age the yeast  is like a fountain of youth  the 500 year old enterprise is a  traditional family operation  i was very lucky with my parents because  they raised me simply as a person and  not as a girl  it was a gender-neutral upbringing i was  taught i could achieve whatever i wanted  the number of women vintners is on the  rise but three generations  is a rarity regina menger kook's mother  is over 90 but still actively involved  and soon daughter marie will take over  a lot will remain the same because my  parents have done a great job  some people i studied with have had  conflicts with the older generation  but my parents have stayed young and fit  they'll be happy to work another 50  years  practical knowledge passed down the  generations and attention to nature  those are the secrets of the success of  regina menger  outstanding sparkling wines  and that is all for this edition of our  euromax highlights and be sure to visit  our website or perhaps  our facebook page if you'd like to catch  up on some of those reports again  otherwise until we meet again all the  best and thanks for watching  cheers  you
 

